# Cloudflare Workers Assets header rules. Copied into build/client/ by Vite,
# because `public/` is the publicDir, and read by the assets runtime.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Workers Assets defaults every asset to
# `cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`. MEASURED on production
# 2026-08-16, on one full document load of /admin/media: 14 asset requests, all
# 14 going to the network, every one returning headers only (transferSize 300
# against encoded bodies of up to 60 kB, so a 304 with the body already on
# disk). Median 689ms each and 1204ms for the slowest, against a document whose
# own response finished at 3146ms. The revalidations, not the HTML, are what
# stood between responseEnd and interactive.
#
# ONLY `/assets/*`, and the narrowness is the whole point. Everything under it
# is Vite build output whose filename CONTAINS its content hash, so the URL
# changes whenever the bytes do and a year is safe by construction.
#
# Nothing else gets this. `logo.svg`, `favicon.ico` and the icon suite sit at
# stable paths with no hash, so an immutable year would make replacing one
# unshippable, and this repo has already recorded browsers holding a stale
# favicon hard enough to look like a failed deploy.
#
# This changes STATIC ASSET caching only. HTML cache policy is untouched: it is
# set per route in the app and governed by hard rule 8.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
